|weaponinfo =
The Beowulf is a variant of the AR-15 designed to fire the proprietary .50 Beowulf (12.7x42mm) cartridge, created and developed by Bill Alexander of Alexander Arms around 2001. The .50 Beowulf is similar to the .500 Smith and Wesson cartridge used in the Smith and Wesson Model 500 and the .50 Action Express used by the Desert Eagle. The main purpose of the .50 Beowulf is for its hunting performance, mainly for hunting common North American game such as deer, moose, and black bears at short-medium ranges. <ref>[[Wikipedia:.50 Beowulf|The Wikipedia article about the .50 Beowulf]]</ref>

The Beowulf cartridge is named after the Beowulf epic, one of the oldest surviving pieces of English literature <ref>[[Wikipedia:Beowulf (hero)|The Wikipedia article about the Beowulf hero]]</ref>.
